{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'cd /workspace && python3 -c \"\nimport torch, time, math\ntorch.set_num_threads(1)\n\n# Permute+contiguous is only 0.07ms - negligible.\n# Let me think about what else to try.\n#\n# Idea: What if we compute p0 and p1 logits together?\n# p0 uses logits A, p1 uses a_p*A + a_m*A''^T\n# The softmax computations are separate and both are O(BHL * L)\n# Softmax is memory-bound for large L. For L=256, BHL=5120, each softmax is ~5120 * 256 * 4 = 5MB\n# That'\"'s small, should be fast.\n#\n# Wait - let me benchmark softmax more carefully.\nb, h, l = 1, 20, 256\nBHL = b * h * l\nlogits = torch.randn(BHL, l)\n\nfor _ in range(5):\n    p = logits.softmax(dim=-1)\nt0 = time.process_time_ns()\nfor _ in range(200):\n    p = logits.softmax(dim=-1)\nt0 = (time.process_time_ns() - t0) / 200\n\n# Theoretical: BHL * L * (exp + sum + div) ≈ 3 * BHL * L FLOPs = 3*5120*256 = 3.9M FLOPs\n# But it's memory bound: 2 reads + 1 write = 3 * BHL * L * 4 bytes = 15.7 MB\n# At 10 GB/s single-thread: ~1.5ms for 15MB\n# Actual might be different with PyTorch overhead.\nprint(f'Softmax (BHL={BHL}, L={l}): {t0/1e6:.3f}ms')\n\n# For L=128\nl2 = 128\nlogits2 = torch.randn(BHL, l2)\nfor _ in range(5):\n    p2 = logits2.softmax(dim=-1)\nt1 = time.process_time_ns()\nfor _ in range(200):\n    p2 = logits2.softmax(dim=-1)\nt1 = (time.process_time_ns() - t1) / 200\nprint(f'Softmax (BHL={BHL}, L={l2}): {t1/1e6:.3f}ms')\n\n# Try with contiguous 4D view\nlogits_4d = torch.randn(b, h, l, l)\nfor _ in range(5):\n    p3 = logits_4d.view(BHL, l).softmax(dim=-1).view(b, h, l, l)\nt2 = time.process_time_ns()\nfor _ in range(200):\n    p3 = logits_4d.view(BHL, l).softmax(dim=-1).view(b, h, l, l)\nt2 = (time.process_time_ns() - t2) / 200\nprint(f'Softmax 4D->view: {t2/1e6:.3f}ms')\n\n# How about 4D softmax directly?\nfor _ in range(5):\n    p4 = logits_4d.softmax(dim=-1)\nt3 = time.process_time_ns()\nfor _ in range(200):\n    p4 = logits_4d.softmax(dim=-1)\nt3 = (time.process_time_ns() - t3) / 200\nprint(f'Softmax 4D direct: {t3/1e6:.3f}ms')\n\\\"\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
